  "what_varies": "The vowel filter is 3 constant-peak band-passes in parallel beside a direct path, each with its own signed weight; the drive stage sits after it.",
  "vowel_is": "The filter fitted on the first printed vowel with the drive stage out. The Vowel byte names that vowel and every value past the printed list, which keeps the state asked before it -- every take of a value past the list asked it straight after 00. The other four printed vowels were never taken where a fit may read them, so no state is named for 01 to 04 and those settings cannot be drawn.",
  "drive_is": "A tanh behind a gain of 20 log10(v / 48) dB, held below byte 3.77 at the state the bottom settings of the overdrive's drive byte share: the drive claim's law on another type, carried here with this type's own printed rest of 48. The gains either side of the curve are fitted at that rest only, so every other drive setting is the carried law's prediction. Drive Sw takes the whole stage out of the path.",
  "fits": {
